## Research Context

This project was developed as part of a university dissertation exploring:

1. **Efficient infinite terrain generation** — chunk streaming, threading, and LOD
2. **Biome-based environmental variation** — configurable, data-driven world design
3. **Optimised vegetation rendering** — GPU instancing at scale
4. **Computational aesthetics** — using photographic composition metrics to evaluate the visual quality of procedurally generated scenes

The photography and scoring system serves as both a data-collection tool and a player feedback mechanism, allowing quantitative evaluation of whether PCG environments produce aesthetically pleasing compositions.

